known communication, because others have known issues. We could challenge that by pointing out that D's known issues (arrogance, hot temper, weak leadership) are equally severe, and that we have evidence that Candidate C is 100% reliable and creates positive atmosphere, which may be more important for long-distance flights. Also C can make correct decisions quickly, calm in crisis (implied). Actually our notes: \"C can make correct decisions quickly.\" Also \"C keeps calm in crisis\"? Not in our notes, but earlier we had \"C keeps calm in crisis\" from earlier? Actually the initial notes: \"Candidate C can make correct decisions quickly.\" and \"Candidate C is regarded as egocentric.\" and \"Candidate C is not very willing to further his education.\" Also \"Candidate C is known to be 100% reliable.\" and \"Candidate C creates a positive atmosphere with his crew.\" So we have reliability and crew positivity.\n\nThus we could argue that C's reliability and crew atmosphere may outweigh D's temperament concerns. Also D's weak leadership may be problematic for long-distance flights.\n\nThus we could shift recommendation to Candidate C.\n\nBut we need to be careful: we must not introduce new facts not in notes. We have \"C creates a positive atmosphere with his crew.\" That's a crew cooperation strength. Also \"C is known to be 100% reliable.\" That's reliability. Also \"C can make correct decisions quickly.\" That's decision quality. Also \"C has difficulty communicating ideas\" is a concern. \"C is egocentric\" also a concern. \"C not willing to further education\" is adaptability concern.\n\nWe need to weigh. D's strengths: concentration, problem solving, responsibility, handling unexpected events. D's concerns: arrogance, hot temper, weak leadership.\n\nWhich is more severe? Hard to decide. As Sarah, we can argue that D's temperament could jeopardize crew cooperation on long flights, while C's proven reliability and positive crew atmosphere suggest better cooperation despite communication difficulty. So we could recommend C.\n\nWe need to reference James and Emily's points: they said D is best because others have known communication issues. We can counter that D's known temperament issues are equally severe, and that we have evidence of C's positive crew atmosphere and reliability, which may be more critical.\n\nThus we will change vote to Candidate C.\n\nWe must include evidence: C 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, can make correct decisions quickly. Also note concerns: difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education. Explain why strengths outweigh concerns relative to D.\n\nThus produce public message: \"I understand James and Emily's support for D, but I think D's arrogance and hot temper, plus weak leadership, pose a higher risk to crew cooperation than C's communication difficulty. C is 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, makes correct decisions quickly, which are crucial for long-distance flights. Therefore I recommend Candidate C.\"\n\nWe must include metadata JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
